## 6. THE GOHIGHLEVEL RELAY IS UNTOUCHED

This is the regression that would actually hurt, so it is asserted rather than argued.

**Argued:** `git diff main -- backend/app/webhooks/bulkvs.py` removes nothing and rewrites
nothing. `await queue.enqueue(db, "message_relay_ghl", {"message_id": str(msg.id)})` is the
same line in the same place, still inside the same session block, still before anything
CRM-related runs. `workers/handlers.handle_message_relay_ghl` is not in the diff at all, and
neither is `handle_message_send`, which enqueues the outbound relay.

**Asserted:** `test_crm_inbound_relay::test_the_existing_gohighlevel_relay_still_enqueues_
exactly_as_it_does_today` drives the REAL route in three worlds — link off; link on with the
DID unbound; link on with the DID BOUND — and in each one checks that

  * the webhook answered 200,
  * there is **exactly one** `message_relay_ghl` job,
  * its payload is **exactly** `{"message_id": str(msg.id)}` and nothing else,
  * and it is the **first** job enqueued, before anything the CRM link does.

A second test asserts the job *sequence* is identical with the module off and on for an
unbound DID, and a third asserts the relay still runs on a re-delivered webhook that the CRM
link correctly skips.

The same shape of assertion covers the DLR route: `test_crm_delivery_receipt::test_owens_own
_row_is_advanced_exactly_as_it_is_today` checks the forward-only advance (`sent` ->
`delivered`, and a late `sent` that must not walk a delivered message back) with the link
both off and on, and that an unrecognised carrier word still leaves the row alone.

