   command that settles it is still `GET /api/crm-link/health` — its `crm_reachable` field.
2. **No real inbound text has ever gone through this.** The BulkVS MO webhook path is driven
   by the real route function against a faked database. `BulkvsAdapter.parse_message_event`
   and `ingest_message_event` are existing, live code and are not changed here, but the
   combination — a real MO POST, ingested, then reported to a real CRM — has not happened.
3. **No real DLR has ever gone through this.** BulkVS's DLR field names for the *failure
   text* are a guess: `_carrier_detail` tries nine plausible keys and returns `""` when it
   recognises none, so a failed message still reports FAILED and the CRM falls back to its
   own wording — "the carrier could not deliver it". `RefId` and `Status` are NOT guesses;
   they are the existing code's, unchanged. The first real failed text is what settles the
   detail key, and finding `""` there is a five-minute fix, not a design problem.
4. **The CRM-link SMS send path is still dark**, so the marker in §5.1 has never been written
   by a real send. `CRM_LINK_SMS_ENABLED=false`, the DID's `sms_enabled` is false, and its
   10DLC campaign is SUBMITTED and unapproved. Which means the delivery-receipt relay has
   nothing to relay until 10DLC lands — it is built and tested ahead of the switch, not in
   use. `providers/bulkvs_client.send_message`'s own note still stands: its `/messageSend`
   request shape has never been exercised against the live BulkVS API.
5. **The CRM's QUEUED -> SENT transition depends on the carrier.** If BulkVS emits no `sent`
   DLR at all, the CRM's copy stays QUEUED until a terminal receipt arrives, because nothing
   relays OWEN's own "the send succeeded" moment — that happens in
   `workers/handlers.handle_message_send`, which I did not touch. If the owner finds
   messages resting on QUEUED in the CRM after a real send, that is the cause, and the fix
   is one `report_delivery_receipt(status="sent")` call in that handler. I left it out
   deliberately: it is a change to a live worker on a path I cannot exercise, and it is not
   needed unless the carrier's behaviour turns out to require it.
6. **The amended CRM is not on ghl-clone's `main`.** See §7. Deploy order matters.

